{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/599511-demon-resort-palm-springs","id":599511,"title":"Demon Resort: Palm Springs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-22T09:38:03-07:00","id":599511,"title":"Demon Resort: Palm Springs","content":"I'll be running a short Demon game soon, and I found the perfect place to set it: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palm_Springs,_California\" target=\"_blank\">Palm Springs, California</a>. Why is it the perfect place?<br /> <br /> Part of it is the aesthetic: Palm Springs was sort of Ground Zero for the development of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mid-Century_modern\" target=\"_blank\">mid-century modern</a> architectural/decoration style. And I associate that style with spy fiction, hence I associate it with Demon.<br /> <br /> Architecture is also very important in Palm Springs. Lots of artists and architects do stuff there, and the city puts a lot of money into <i>construction</i>, <i>reconstruction</i>, and having famous artists <i>design weird floorplans</i>. In other words? A perfect place to lay down some Infrastructure. There could be a major God-Machine cult with low-level initiates being wide-eyed architecture students coming in to an organization dedicated to helping them develop their skills, and the cult leaders throwing lavish parties for lobbyists and city planners.<br /> <br /> I also picked Palm Springs because I've been listening to a lot of Welcome to Nightvale, and I was just in the mood for a desert setting. But wait, what's that? <a href=\"http://www.desertsun.com/story/news/crime_courts/2015/07/14/devillena-shooting-court-documents/30150189/\" target=\"_blank\">The police force is crazy?</a> Well, that sounds like there's something weird going on with the police force. Maybe there's a mystery cult led by an angel known as The Sheriff. Perhaps the Sheriff's Secret Poilce.<br /> <br /> I asked around the Palm Springs subreddit for some urban legends and other story hooks, and discovered that there's a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tahquitz_Canyon\" target=\"_blank\">nearby canyon with a mythological history</a> (cryptid? angel? demon? something else?), a hidden &quot;Midget Town&quot; somewhere down 111 (Facility), &quot;skinwalkers&quot; associated with Joshua Tree National Park (definitely cryptids), and potentially a network of mob tunnels hidden under the city.<br /> <br /> Given Palm Springs's reputation as a major tourist destination and home for celebrities, I figure the primary agency there would be a Tempter-led organization mostly about collecting Covers belonging to the rich and famous (I call 'em the Fallen Stars) and their Entourages.<br /> <br /> I'm writing up NPCs and hooks and such presently. Would people like me to post that when it's done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},